 :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286124} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf1ee90-91fd-5d48-9ae2-5efc13ddabc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287102} {:answer/id #uuid "ff08aaf7-5fe4-5d35-a694-3337c9df4aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287126}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286124} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb288b6a-0ce0-5325-bbb2-0ee9ec1811d7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2898c964-611b-56ce-8ed9-635cb443e151" :question/math-academy-id "q-181685" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2d1c647ec7899221567d67e24e90a9f1efca60650b82a739e843e4085be636e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,2x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,-x+3\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=2x$ and *below* the line $y=-x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>2x,\\,y<-x+3.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n2x<y<-x+3.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x<y<-x+3\\}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0e86ea9a-9531-5eb8-9292-ae72f3485efe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420384}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420382 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "155eddcc-7b10-5882-9c3b-e997a278e33e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759