f3beaf2d933fb03cfbe69f510ca5b68f1fd861f83.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,-x+1\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x+1.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x+1\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny>-x+1.\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>-x+1\\}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9666f8df-4f8e-5149-a6a4-0197ed8b36ff" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420383}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420383 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18ff83ff-a85e-5759-9a2a-3d799b7146cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285009} {:answer/id #uuid "22dcd8b2-76cb-51d8-aa88-be7ec7d0f316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285101} {:answer/id #uuid "31cf8ca8-2c9c-5660-b2d4-d28776812fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285240} {:answer/id #uuid "888939e6-2972-505a-a344-1b5368a90f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285009} :answer-field/id #uuid "15922b56-5dee-5494-8dfc-80286a88342e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e641f7d-97d5-592f-b908-a83d570e3900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :an